+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The Guarantor step's text fields (name, phone, email, income, employer) reject browser autofill — the browser suggests entries but clicking them does not populate the fields. Root cause: `form_fields.autocomplete_for` stamps `autocomplete="off"` (an explicit autofill opt-out) on every field not in an 8-name whitelist (`first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `phone`, `current_address`, `current_city`, `current_county`, `eircode`). All five guarantor fields hit the `_ -> "off"` fallback. The whitelisted sections (About You contact trio, Situation address quartet) are exactly the ones that autofill today; the same bug silently affects references, work/income, co-applicant, and additional-income fields. The JS layer is clean: the cohort module only writes `_guarantor_*` synthetic hidden inputs, the condition engine only toggles `el.hidden`, and no handler clobbers field values.
+
+**Approach:** Give every form text field a proper HTML `autocomplete` token via a suffix-aware mapping in `autocomplete_for` (exact names first, then suffix rules covering both bare and bracket-prefixed `co_applicant[N][...]` / `additional_income[N][...]` names), keeping `"off"` only for fields with no standard token (dates, counts, free text). Pure SSR attribute change — no JS, no conditional-logic changes.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Every text field gets a semantically correct token: `_name` → `name`, `_email` → `email`, `_phone` → `tel`, `_employer` / `employer_name` → `organization`, `_monthly_income_cents` / `amount` → `transaction-amount`, `job_title` → `organization-title`. First/last name keep `given-name`/`family-name`; address quartet keeps its current tokens.
+- `"off"` remains ONLY for token-less fields (`desired_move_in_date`, `num_occupants`, `pet_details`, `reason_for_moving`, `employment_duration`, `eviction_details`, income notes, `additional_income[N][note]`, `co_applicant[N][note]`) and the honeypot.
+- No changes to `data-condition` engine, cohort module, hidden-state logic, field names, IDs, or types. Conditional show/hide must behave exactly as before (guarantor hidden when not required, visible when required).
+- `autocomplete_for` stays a pure function; bracket-prefixed names normalize to their inner field name before matching so one rule set covers bare and prefixed fields.
+
+**Ask First:** None expected — the briefing prescribes the tokens.
+
+**Never:** No JS changes; no DOM behavior changes; no autofill tokens on file inputs or the honeypot; no changing `view_select_field` / `view_textarea_field` (selects get no autocomplete attr, textareas stay token-free).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| BARE_CONTACT | `guarantor_name`, `guarantor_phone`, `guarantor_email` | `name`, `tel`, `email` | n/a |
+| BARE_ORG_AMOUNT | `guarantor_employer`, `employer_name`, `guarantor_monthly_income_cents`, `monthly_income_cents` | `organization`, `organization`, `transaction-amount`, `transaction-amount` | n/a |
+| SUFFIX_ONLY | `landlord_ref_name`, `character_ref_phone`, `employer_ref_email` | `name`, `tel`, `email` | n/a |
+| BRACKETED | `co_applicant[0][first_name]`, `co_applicant[2][guarantor_email]`, `additional_income[1][amount]` | `given-name`, `email`, `transaction-amount` | n/a |
+| NAME_VS_ORG | `employer_name` (org) vs `employer_ref_name` (person) | `organization` vs `name` — exact match wins before suffix `_name` | n/a |
+| TOKENLESS | `desired_move_in_date`, `pet_details`, `reason_for_moving` | `off` | n/a |
+| WHITELIST_KEPT | `first_name`, `email`, `current_address`, `eircode` | `given-name`, `email`, `street-address`, `postal-code` (unchanged) | n/a |
