+## Spec Change Log
+
+- 2026-08-05 (Perkins r1 B1): the AC named all three guarantor fields while the Design Notes documented Chromium's 9-per-type fill cap — internal contradiction, and the cap makes the name/email AC unsatisfiable from the form side (no alternative standard tokens; the co-applicant cards are the multiplier). Amended the AC per human ruling [A]: `guarantor_phone` + `guarantor_employer` populate; `guarantor_name`/`guarantor_email` carved out explicitly with the cap rationale (10th NAME_FULL / 11th EMAIL instance) and the carve-out acceptance (correct tokens + Chrome classifies them). Residual stated in the PR title/description. Follow-up [B] (co-applicant-card de-dup, the real lever) appended to deferred-work for v1.1. KEEP: the `tel`/`tel-national` split — the only honest token lever, verified in Chrome 150, and the HTML-level pin added for it.
+
+## Design Notes
+
+Golden mapping examples (bare → suffix → bracket-normalized):
+
+```
+guarantor_name            -> name            (suffix _name)
+employer_name             -> organization    (exact — NOT _name)
+co_applicant[0][first_name] -> given-name    (normalize to first_name, exact)
+co_applicant[2][guarantor_employer] -> organization (normalize, suffix _employer)
+additional_income[1][amount] -> transaction-amount (normalize to amount, exact)
+desired_move_in_date      -> off             (no standard token)
+```
+
+`name` (not `given-name`) is correct for single "Full name" fields per the HTML spec — Chrome fills it from the profile's full name. `transaction-amount` is the only standard token for currency amounts; Chrome has no income profile field, so the token's job is to stop `off` suppressing form-fillers.
+
+**Chromium per-type fill cap (discovered in real-browser verification, 2026-08-05):**
+Chromium's `kTypeValueFormFillingLimit = 9` (`autofill_constants.h`) — at most 9 fields per type fill per fill action, counted across the whole form in DOM order (`form_filler.cc` `GetFillingSkipReasonsForField`). The apply form's contact repetition (About You + 3 reference trios + 3 co-applicant cards × employer/guarantor blocks) makes the primary guarantor block the 10th NAME_FULL / 11th PHONE / 11th EMAIL instance — Chrome suppresses those three on every fill action, which reproduces the reported bug exactly (other sections fill; the guarantor trio doesn't; the employer at COMPANY count 8 fills). Counts verified against Chrome 150's autofill-internals fill records.
+
+**The one honest token lever:** `tel` vs `tel-national` are separate Chrome type buckets. Co-applicant phones map to `tel-national` (standard WHATWG token — national-format phone), keeping the primary block at 5 `tel` and co-applicant blocks at 6 `tel-national` — every phone in the form is fillable (verified: guarantor_phone fills). NAME and EMAIL have no alternative standard tokens, so the guarantor name/email remain subject to the cap — a Chromium limit, not a form defect; the lever is a product decision (reduce co-applicant card duplication) if it ever matters.
+
